  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday Night through Thursday)\nIssued at 1140 PM CDT Thu Oct 15 2026\n\nLingering low clouds over the Ozarks Friday night are expected to\nhold low temps up around 40 degrees and will prevent frost \nconditions from developing. However, to the west of the expected\nlow cloud shield across far NE OK near the KS border, low temps in\nthe mid 30s are expected to support frost development. A frost\nadvisory will be needed with the next forecast update if this\ntrend continues. Clouds are not expected to be a factor by\nSaturday night, and with the surface ridge either close by or\noverhead, conditions may be favorable in more areas for frost\ndevelopment.\n\nA warming trend will commence over the weekend with ridging aloft\nand at the surface maintaining quiet weather. This warming trend\nwill continue sharply upward as we head into next week, with 80\ndegree highs returning Wednesday. An upper trough is expected to \nbecome established over the western CONUS with downstream ridging \nover the Plains. Dry weather is expected to persist until the \nupper trough starts its trek toward the Plains. The latest \nensemble data suggests this may not happen until the end of next \nweek.\n\nLacy",
